; DOMAIN: mathematics/number-theory/algebraic-geometry/descent [CLOSED, derived 2026-08-02]; Claim: Descent theory provides a framework for gluing objects and morphisms from local to global using covering data. Key concepts: faithfully flat descent (fpqc/fppf topologies) classifying quasi-coherent sheaves and modules via descent data along faithfully flat morphisms; effective descent morphisms satisfying a compositional lifting condition; Galois descent (forms classified by H^1(G, Aut(X))); nonabelian H^1 classifying twists under torsors; Grothendieck-Galois correspondence between finite étale covers and continuous Galois sets; the cocycle condition ensuring well-defined gluing. Bridges to galois_cohomology (H^1, nonabelian H^1, twisted forms), algebraic_geometry (schemes, fiber products, étale morphisms), and sheaf_cohomology (Čech descent).;; Faithfully flat descent: quasi-coherent sheaves and modules classified by descent data along faithfully flat morphisms (fpqc/fppf topologies)
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Scheme $S) (--> FaithfullyFlatMorphism $f $X $S) (--> QuasiCoherentSheaf $F) (--> DescentData $F $f) (--> EffectiveDescent $f))) (--> FaithfullyFlatDescent $f $F))) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Effective descent morphism: satisfies compositional lifting condition, descent data along f is effective (glues uniquely)
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Morphism $f $X $S) (--> CompositionalLifting $f) (--> GluesUniquely (DescentData $f)))) (--> EffectiveDescentMorphism $f))) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Galois descent: forms of an object X over a field k classified by H^1(Gal(k^sep/k), Aut(X_{k^sep}))
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Field $k) (--> SeparableClosure $k_sep) (--> GaloisGroup $G $k) (--> Object $X) (--> AutomorphismGroup $Aut (BaseChange $X $k_sep)) (--> ClassifiedBy (Forms $X $k) (H1 $G $Aut)))) (--> GaloisDescent $k $X))) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Nonabelian H^1: classifies twists of X under G-torsors, generalizes Galois cohomology to nonabelian coefficient groups
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Group $G) (--> NonabelianGroup $A) (--> Torsor $T $G $A) (--> TwistedForm $X $T) (--> ClassifiedBy (Twists $X) (H1 $G $A)))) (--> NonabelianH1 $G $A))) (stv 1.0 0.9)
;; Grothendieck-Galois correspondence: finite étale covers of a connected scheme correspond to continuous finite sets with Galois group action
(|- ((==> (&& (--> ConnectedScheme $S) (--> FiniteEtaleCover $X $S) (--> GaloisGroup $G $S) (--> ContinuousAction $G $F) (--> Equivalent (CategoryOf $X) (CategoryOf $F)))) (--> GrothendieckGaloisCorrespondence $S))) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Cocycle condition: descent data must satisfy compatibility on triple fiber products ensuring well-defined gluing
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Morphism $f $X $S) (--> DescentData $phi $f) (--> TripleFiberProduct $X3) (--> Satisfies $phi (CocycleCondition $X3)))) (--> ValidDescentData $phi $f))) (stv 1.0 0.9))
